2. Test Process

The test process is a systematic sequence of activities used to plan, prepare, execute, and complete software testing.

A commonly used testing process has seven activities.

1 Test Planning

Define objectives, scope, resources and schedule.

2 Test Monitoring and Control

Track progress and take corrective action.

3 Test Analysis

Identify what needs to be tested.

4 Test Design

Decide how to test and define test cases.

5n Test Implementation

Prepare test data, test procedures and test environment.

6 Test Execution

Run tests, compare actual and expected results, and report defects.

7 Test Completion

Summarize results, document lessons learned and close testing activities.
